#: conf.json:summary
msgid "Differential correctness and performance benchmarks for Luna-Flow MoonBit packages."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/core.md:1
msgid "core API"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/core.md:3
msgid "The package `Luna-Flow/diff_bench` at the source root (`src/`) holds the module's template placeholder. The benchmarks live in the subpackages [`dzmingli_vs_floating`](dzmingli_vs_floating.md) and [`floating_vs_decmial_x`](floating_vs_decmial_x.md)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/core.md:10
msgid "`hello` returns the fixed greeting `\"hello from Luna-Flow\"`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/core.md:16
msgid "It takes no input, has no side effects and never fails. It exists so that the root package has a public item and a test; no benchmark uses it."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:1
msgid "dzmingli_vs_floating API"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:3
msgid "The package `Luna-Flow/diff_bench/dzmingli_vs_floating` compares `DzmingLi/decimal@0.2.2` with `Luna-Flow/floating/decimal_gda@0.7.1` on identical decimal inputs, checks both against an exact `BigInt` oracle, and measures them with Mare Mark. It is a benchmark harness, not a decimal library: every function aborts on input outside its contract instead of returning a `Result`, because an invalid fixture is a bug in the harness."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:10
msgid "The [tutorial](../tutorial/dzmingli_vs_floating.md) shows the items in use, and the [design page](../design/dzmingli_vs_floating.md) derives the precision contract and the oracle. Source: `src/dzmingli_vs_floating/`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:14
msgid "The examples on this page are blackbox tests: they import the package as `@dzmingli_vs_floating` and `moonbitlang/core/bigint`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:17
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:18
msgid "Neutral decimal model"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:21
msgid "`DecimalValue` is the implementation-neutral decimal that every fixture, oracle result and observation is converted to."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:31
msgid "A value $(c, s)$ denotes $c \\cdot 10^{-s}$. The sign lives in the coefficient. Values produced by this package have $s \\ge 0$; a negative exponent is multiplied into the coefficient by `parse_decimal_value`. Many pairs denote the same number, such as $(1200, 2)$ and $(12, 0)$; `normalize` picks one of them."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:39
msgid "`normalize` removes trailing decimal zeros from the coefficient while the scale stays non-negative."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:46
msgid "Zero becomes $(0, 0)$. For any other value the result has $s = 0$ or a coefficient not divisible by $10$. That form is unique for each number, so two values are equal exactly when their normalized forms are equal (proof in the [design page](../design/dzmingli_vs_floating.md#correctness-and-invariants)). Cost: one `BigInt` division per removed zero."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:54
msgid "`canonical_string` renders the normalized value in plain positional notation, without an exponent."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:61
msgid "The string has a leading `-` for negative values, a `0.` prefix and leading fractional zeros when $|v| < 1$, and no trailing zeros. It is injective on numbers, so string equality is value equality. This string is the comparison boundary for every validation in the package."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:68
msgid "`parse_decimal_value` reads a finite decimal string into a normalized `DecimalValue`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:75
msgid "Accepted syntax: an optional leading sign, digits with at most one `.`, and an optional exponent `e` or `E` with its own optional sign. Digits are accumulated into a `BigInt` one at a time, so the parser does not depend on `BigInt::from_string`. It aborts on an empty digit sequence, an exponent without digits, `NaN`, `Infinity` or any other character. The exponent is held in an `Int`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:84
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:65
msgid "`OracleResult` holds a normalized value and its canonical string."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:95
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:76
msgid "`to_oracle_result` normalizes a value and pairs it with its canonical string."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:113
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:93
msgid "Exact arithmetic"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:115
msgid "These functions compute exactly on `DecimalValue`; there is no precision and no rounding. Results are normalized."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:120
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:97
msgid "`add` returns the exact sum after aligning both operands to the larger scale."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:128
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:105
msgid "`subtract` returns the exact difference after the same alignment."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:136
msgid "`multiply` returns the exact product: coefficients multiply and scales add."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:144
msgid "`compare` returns `-1`, `0` or `1` as the left operand is less than, equal to or greater than the right one."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:163
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:139
msgid "Reference oracle"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:165
msgid "The oracle computes the expected result of every benchmarked operation exactly, with `BigInt` arithmetic only. Its semantics are those of a GDA context with enough precision and rounding toward zero; the [design page](../design/dzmingli_vs_floating.md#the-exact-finite-oracle) states each rule."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:173
msgid "`oracle_multiply` returns the exact product; it is `multiply` under the oracle's name."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:182
msgid "`oracle_divide` returns the exact quotient when it has a finite decimal expansion."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:189
msgid "It aborts on a zero divisor and on a quotient whose reduced denominator has a prime factor other than $2$ and $5$ (\"repeating decimal in exact decimal oracle\"). Cost: a `BigInt` GCD plus one multiplication by $10$ per fractional digit of the result."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:196
msgid "`oracle_operation` evaluates a binary or unary `Operation` and returns the normalized result."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:203
msgid "It is `oracle_operation3` with a zero third operand, so it gives the wrong answer for `Fma` unless the addend is zero."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:208
msgid "`oracle_operation3` evaluates any `Operation`; the third operand is the addend of `Fma` and is ignored otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:215
#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:477
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:412
msgid "Operation"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:215
msgid "Expected value"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:217
msgid "exact result"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:218
msgid "exact terminating quotient; aborts otherwise"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:219
msgid "quotient truncated toward zero"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:220
msgid "$a - b \\cdot \\operatorname{trunc}(a/b)$, with the sign of $a$"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:221
msgid "$a^n$ by repeated multiplication; $n$ must be a non-negative integer"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:222
msgid "$a \\cdot b + c$ exactly"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:223
msgid "exact root of a perfect square with an even scale; aborts otherwise"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:225
msgid "$a$ truncated toward zero to the scale of $b$"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:226
msgid "$a$ truncated toward zero to scale $-b$; $b$ must be an integer"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:227
msgid "$a \\cdot 10^{b}$; $b$ must be an integer"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:228
msgid "normalized $a$"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:229
msgid "$a$ truncated toward zero to an integer"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:230
msgid "`-1`, `0` or `1` as a decimal"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:231
msgid "$a$ unchanged"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:248
msgid "Operations and suites"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:252
msgid "`Operation` lists the operation families of the benchmark."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:280
msgid "`Parse` and `Format` are identity paths: both adapters return the prepared left operand, so they measure nothing and are not run by the executables."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:285
msgid "`operation_name` returns the stable snake-case name used in JSONL records and fingerprints, such as `\"divide_integer\"` or `\"sqrt\"`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:294
msgid "`OperandShape` labels a generated case."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:306
msgid "The label is serialized into the case and its fingerprint; `generate_cases` assigns it cyclically by index and it does not change how operands are generated."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:312
msgid "`TimingScope` selects what a timed invocation contains."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:321
msgid "`OperationOnly` times the public operation on operands prepared before timing. `FullPath` also parses both canonical operand strings, and the addend for `Fma`, under the prepared context."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:327
msgid "`timing_scope_name` returns `\"arithmetic_only\"` or `\"full_path\"`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:335
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:286
msgid "`Suite` is descriptive metadata for a benchmark suite."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:350
msgid "`default_suite` returns the suite named `\"dzmingli-vs-floating-gda\"` with all 21 operations, scales `[0, 2, 6, 18, 28]`, `OperationOnly`, 5 warmups and 20 samples. The Mare Mark runners do not read it; their protocol comes from `default_benchmark_protocol`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:361
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:311
msgid "`suite_case_count` returns operations × scales × cases per operation."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:376
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:326
msgid "Deterministic cases"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:380
msgid "`generate_decimal(seed, digits, scale, negative)` builds a decimal string with exactly `digits` coefficient digits, `scale` of them after the point."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:387
msgid "Digit $i$ is $1 + ((\\mathit{seed} + 7i) \\bmod 9)$, so every digit is in $1..9$: the coefficient has exactly `digits` digits and no trailing zero. When `scale >= digits` the string starts with `0.` and leading zeros. Aborts if `digits <= 0` or `scale < 0`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:394
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:340
msgid "`BenchmarkCase` is a generated case; its strings are the serialization boundary."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:410
msgid "`generate_cases(seed, count, operation)` returns `count` reproducible cases without reading the clock or global random state."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:417
msgid "Case $i$ has $1 + ((\\mathit{seed} + 11i) \\bmod 24)$ digits and scale $(\\mathit{seed} + 5i) \\bmod 9$ for both operands. Divisors are not filtered, so `Divide` cases may not terminate; use them with the adapters, not with `oracle_divide`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:424
msgid "`serialize_case` joins the version tag `decimal-neutral-v1`, the id, the operation name, the shape name, both operands and the scale with newlines."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:433
msgid "`fingerprint_case` hashes `serialize_case` with Mare Mark's `stable_fingerprint` and returns a `sha256:` string."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:442
msgid "`expand_digit_scales(sizes, n)` repeats each coefficient size `n` times, so that Mare Mark creates `n` independent datasets per size."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:463
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:399
msgid "Fixtures and adapters"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:467
msgid "`working_precision` returns a number of significant digits large enough for the exact result of an operation on the given operands."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:474
msgid "With $d_\\ell, d_r$ the digit counts of the coefficients and $s_\\ell, s_r$ the scales:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:477
msgid "Result"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:481
msgid "`SquareRoot` and the unary operations"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:484
msgid "`prepare_fixture3` adds two guard digits and overrides `Power` and `Fma`; the [design page](../design/dzmingli_vs_floating.md#precision-contract) proves which operand classes each bound covers."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:490
msgid "`DecimalFixture` holds both implementations' operands and contexts, built before timing."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:510
msgid "`@decimal` is `DzmingLi/decimal` and `@decimal_gda` is `Luna-Flow/floating/decimal_gda`. The `*_text` fields are the canonical strings that `FullPath` parses again."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:516
msgid "`prepare_fixture3(operation, left, right, third)` chooses the precision $p$, builds both contexts with precision $p$ and rounding toward zero, and parses all three canonical strings into both libraries."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:524
msgid "$p$ is $2 d_\\ell + 4$ for `Power`, $d_\\ell + d_r + d_t + \\lvert s_\\ell + s_r - s_t \\rvert + 4$ for `Fma`, and `working_precision(...) + 2` otherwise. Aborts if DzmingLi reports a conversion-syntax error."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:531
msgid "`prepare_fixture(operation, left, right)` is `prepare_fixture3` with a zero third operand."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:540
msgid "`dz_from_neutral` converts a value to a DzmingLi decimal under `Context::exact()`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:549
msgid "`gda_from_neutral(value, precision)` parses the canonical string into a GDA decimal under a context with the given precision and rounding toward zero."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:558
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:480
msgid "`DecimalObservation` is the raw result of one adapter call."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:567
msgid "The GDA variant keeps the whole outcome, including flags and the next context; validation reads only its value."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:572
msgid "`run_dz` performs the fixture's operation with DzmingLi on the prepared operands. This is the `OperationOnly` timed body."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:581
msgid "`run_dz_full` parses the fixture's three strings under `dz_context` and then performs the operation. This is the `FullPath` timed body."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:590
msgid "`run_gda` performs the fixture's operation with floating GDA on the prepared operands."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:599
msgid "`run_gda_full` parses the fixture's three strings under `gda_context` and then performs the operation."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:608
msgid "`canonical_observation` converts an observation to a normalized `DecimalValue`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:615
msgid "DzmingLi results go through `to_sci_string`, GDA results through `to_string`, and both through `parse_decimal_value`. Exponent, trailing zeros and status flags are dropped. Aborts on a NaN or infinite result."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:637
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:545
msgid "Mare Mark integration"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:641
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:549
msgid "`MareDecimalInput` is the materialized input of one Mare Mark dataset."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:658
msgid "`PerformanceResult` summarizes one operation, timing scope and coefficient size."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:676
msgid "`correctness_valid` is true when every validation at that size passed for both implementations. Then the medians come from paired confirmatory samples, `dz_speedup_vs_gda` is the GDA median divided by the DzmingLi median (above $1$ means DzmingLi is faster), `gda_relative_delta_pct` is the median paired difference relative to the DzmingLi median, and `decision` is `\"gda_faster\"`, `\"dzmingli_faster\"`, `\"equivalent\"`, `\"invalid\"` or `\"unknown\"`. Otherwise the medians use each implementation's own valid samples, the speedup and delta are `0.0` and `decision` is `\"invalid_correctness\"`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:688
msgid "`PerformanceResult::to_json` renders a `\"comparison\"` JSONL record tagged with the Mare Mark artifact version `mmka_1`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:697
msgid "`MareBenchmarkReport` collects the results, the raw JSONL and the validation counts of a run."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:709
msgid "`validation_count` counts every oracle validation, passed or failed."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:713
msgid "`smoke_protocol` returns a short Mare Mark protocol for tests: 2 warmups, 0.5 ms calibration batches and 3 confirmatory repetitions."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:722
msgid "`default_benchmark_protocol` returns the protocol of the published runs: 5 warmups, 5 ms calibration batches, balanced block order with seed `0xDEC1A1`, outliers reported but not removed, validation of every dataset and 20 confirmatory repetitions."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:733
msgid "`benchmark_environment` builds the environment snapshot recorded in the JSONL from the `MARE_*` environment variables."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:740
msgid "It reads `MARE_TARGET`, `MARE_COMPILER`, `MARE_BUILD_MODE`, `MARE_CPU`, `MARE_DEVICE`, `MARE_FREQUENCY_POLICY`, `MARE_OS`, `MARE_EXECUTION_CONTEXT` and `MARE_REPOSITORY_STATE`. Missing or empty variables become `unknown`, `unspecified` or another fixed default; nothing is detected from the host."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:747
msgid "`run_mare_benchmark(operations, scope, digit_scales, protocol, seed)` runs one Mare Mark experiment per operation and returns the combined report."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:754
msgid "Each entry of `digit_scales` is one dataset; repeat sizes with `expand_digit_scales`. Every dataset is validated against the oracle before it is timed. The function does not abort on validation failures; callers check `failed_count`. It needs an async runtime, so it runs on the `native` and `js` targets."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:776
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:667
msgid "Reports"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:780
msgid "`mare_performance_report_document(results, target, run_id)` builds a Mare Mark Plot IR document: one latency plot per operation and timing scope, and one DzmingLi-versus-GDA speedup plot per timing scope."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:788
msgid "Sizes where `correctness_valid` is false keep the GDA latency point but contribute no DzmingLi point and no speedup point. The corpus summary is total `validation_count`, passed `validation_count - failed_count` and failed `failed_count`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/dzmingli_vs_floating.md:795
#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:686
msgid "`mare_performance_report_html` renders the same document as a self-contained HTML page."
msgstr ""

