#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:1
msgid "floating_vs_decmial_x API"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:3
msgid "The package `Luna-Flow/diff_bench/floating_vs_decmial_x` compares `moonbitlang/x/decimal` (X) with `Luna-Flow/floating/decimal_gda@0.7.1` (GDA) on identical decimal inputs, checks both against a `BigInt` oracle, and measures them with Mare Mark. It is a benchmark harness kept in the GitHub repository for reproduction; it is not a runtime dependency for other projects. Functions abort on input outside their contract."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:10
msgid "The package name keeps the historical spelling `decmial`. The [tutorial](../tutorial/floating_vs_decmial_x.md) shows the items in use, and the [design page](../design/floating_vs_decmial_x.md) derives the precision contracts. Source: `src/floating_vs_decmial_x/`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:15
msgid "Examples import the package as `@floating_vs_decmial_x` and `moonbitlang/core/bigint`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:20
msgid "These items have the same definitions as in [`dzmingli_vs_floating`](dzmingli_vs_floating.md#neutral-decimal-model); the two packages keep separate copies so that each benchmark builds alone."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:26
msgid "`DecimalValue` is the implementation-neutral decimal $(c, s)$ with value $c \\cdot 10^{-s}$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:38
msgid "`normalize` removes trailing zeros from the coefficient while the scale stays non-negative; zero becomes $(0, 0)$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:47
msgid "`canonical_string` renders the normalized value in positional notation without an exponent; equal numbers give equal strings."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:56
msgid "`parse_decimal_value` reads a finite decimal string, with optional sign, point and exponent, into a normalized value. It aborts on anything else."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:113
msgid "`multiply` returns the exact product."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:121
msgid "`compare` returns `-1`, `0` or `1`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:141
msgid "The oracle models X's result policy: at most 28 fractional digits, extra digits truncated toward zero."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:146
msgid "`oracle_multiply` returns the exact product, truncated toward zero to 28 fractional digits when its scale exceeds 28."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:155
msgid "`oracle_divide` returns the quotient truncated toward zero to 28 fractional digits, computed with integer division only."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:162
msgid "With $k = 28 + s_r - s_\\ell$ the result coefficient is $\\operatorname{trunc}(c_\\ell \\cdot 10^{k} / c_r)$ when $k \\ge 0$ and $\\operatorname{trunc}(\\operatorname{trunc}(c_\\ell / 10^{-k}) / c_r)$ otherwise, at scale 28. Aborts on a zero divisor. Repeating quotients are fine here, unlike in `dzmingli_vs_floating`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:170
msgid "`oracle_operation` evaluates an `Operation` with the rules above: exact `Add`, `Subtract` and `Compare`, the truncating `Multiply` and `Divide`, and the identity for `Parse` and `Format`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:178
msgid "The oracle does not depend on `DecimalSemantics`; the [design page](../design/floating_vs_decmial_x.md#one-oracle-for-both-groups) shows why one oracle serves both groups."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:199
msgid "Operations, semantics and suites"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:203
msgid "`Operation` lists the operation families of this benchmark."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:217
msgid "`Parse` and `Format` return the prepared left operand on both sides and are not run by the executables."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:222
msgid "`operation_name` returns the snake-case name used in records, such as `\"divide\"`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:231
msgid "`DecimalSemantics` selects the semantic contract both implementations must meet."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:241
msgid "`ExactOverlap` uses inputs whose exact result both libraries represent, so no rounding happens on either side. `XCompatible` reproduces X's 28-fractional-digit truncation in GDA by a `quantize` after `multiply` and `divide`, inside the timed path."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:248
msgid "`decimal_semantics_name` returns `\"exact_overlap\"` or `\"x_compatible\"`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:256
msgid "`OperandShape` labels a generated case; the label does not influence the operands."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:271
msgid "`TimingScope` names what a timed invocation contains, for suite metadata."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:280
msgid "The Mare Mark runner does not read it. Comparison records carry a string scope instead: `\"semantic_equivalent_pipeline\"` for `Multiply` and `Divide` under `XCompatible`, `\"arithmetic_only\"` otherwise."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:301
msgid "`default_suite` returns the suite `\"decimal-x-floating-gda\"` with all seven operations, scales `[0, 2, 6, 18, 28]`, `OperationOnly`, 5 warmups and 20 samples."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:330
msgid "`generate_decimal(seed, digits, scale, negative)` builds a decimal string with exactly `digits` coefficient digits in $1..9$, `scale` of them fractional. Aborts if `digits <= 0` or `scale < 0`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:356
msgid "`generate_cases(seed, count, operation)` returns `count` reproducible cases with $1..24$ digits and scales $0..8$, without clock or global random state."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:365
msgid "`serialize_case` joins `decimal-neutral-v1` and the case fields with newlines."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:373
msgid "`fingerprint_case` hashes `serialize_case` with Mare Mark's `stable_fingerprint`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:382
msgid "`expand_digit_scales(sizes, n)` repeats each coefficient size `n` times, one Mare Mark dataset per repetition."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:403
msgid "`working_precision(operation, left, right, semantics?)` returns the GDA context precision of a fixture. `semantics` defaults to `XCompatible`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:410
msgid "With $d_\\ell, d_r$ the coefficient digit counts and $s_\\ell, s_r$ the scales:"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:412
msgid "Precision"
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:420
msgid "The [design page](../design/floating_vs_decmial_x.md#precision-contracts) derives each line and the operand classes it covers."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:425
msgid "`DecimalFixture` holds both implementations' operands, built before timing."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:442
msgid "`@decimal` is `moonbitlang/x/decimal`. `gda_quantum_28` is $10^{-28}$, the quantum of the `XCompatible` post-processing."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:447
msgid "`prepare_fixture(operation, left, right, semantics?)` computes the precision $p$, converts both operands for X and for GDA, and builds a GDA context with precision $p$ and rounding toward zero."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:455
msgid "`semantics` defaults to `XCompatible`. The GDA operands are parsed with precision $p$ and half-even rounding, so an operand with more than $p$ significant digits is rounded; see the [known limitation](../design/floating_vs_decmial_x.md#known-limitation-operand-rounding-in-x-compatible-division)."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:462
msgid "`x_from_neutral` converts a value with `Decimal::new`; it aborts when the scale is outside X's range $0..28$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:471
msgid "`gda_from_neutral(value, precision)` parses the canonical string with `Decimal::from_string(precision~)`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:490
msgid "`XCompare` holds X's comparison result already reduced to `-1`, `0` or `1`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:494
msgid "`run_x` performs the fixture's operation with X's operators `+`, `-`, `*`, `/` or `Compare::compare`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:503
msgid "`run_gda` performs the fixture's operation with floating GDA; under `XCompatible` it also quantizes products whose scale exceeds 28 and every quotient to $10^{-28}$."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:513
msgid "`canonical_x` converts an X decimal to a normalized `DecimalValue` from its coefficient and scale."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:522
msgid "`canonical_observation` converts any observation to a normalized `DecimalValue`; GDA results go through `to_string` and `parse_decimal_value`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:565
msgid "`PerformanceResult` summarizes one operation, semantic group and coefficient size from paired confirmatory samples."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:583
msgid "`x_speedup_vs_gda` is the GDA median divided by the X median (above $1$ means X is faster). `decision` is `\"gda_faster\"`, `\"x_faster\"`, `\"equivalent\"`, `\"invalid\"` or `\"unknown\"`. Unlike `dzmingli_vs_floating`, results are always paired; a validation failure shows up only in the report counts."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:590
msgid "`PerformanceResult::to_json` renders a `\"comparison\"` JSONL record with artifact version `mmka_1`."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:599
msgid "`MareBenchmarkReport` collects the results, raw JSONL and validation counts of a run; `validation_count` counts passed and failed validations."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:613
msgid "`smoke_protocol` returns the short test protocol: 2 warmups, 0.5 ms calibration batches and 3 confirmatory repetitions."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:622
msgid "`default_benchmark_protocol` returns the protocol of the published runs: 5 warmups, 5 ms calibration batches, balanced blocks with seed `0xDEC1A1`, outliers reported only, and 20 confirmatory repetitions."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:632
msgid "`benchmark_environment` builds the environment snapshot from the `MARE_*` environment variables, with fixed defaults for missing ones."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:641
msgid "`run_mare_benchmark(operations, semantics, digit_scales, protocol, seed)` runs one Mare Mark experiment per operation under one semantic group and returns the combined report."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:649
msgid "Each dataset is validated against the oracle before timing. The function does not abort on failures; callers check `failed_count`. It runs on the `native` and `js` targets."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:671
msgid "`mare_performance_report_document(results, target, run_id)` builds a Plot IR document with one latency plot per operation and semantic group, and one X-versus-GDA speedup plot per group."
msgstr ""

#: manual/api/floating_vs_decmial_x.md:679
msgid "The corpus summary is total `validation_count + failed_count`, passed `validation_count` and failed `failed_count`. Because `validation_count` already includes failures, the summary is only right when `failed_count` is zero; see the [design page](../design/floating_vs_decmial_x.md#boundaries)."
msgstr ""

